&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior z/OS Base System Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;As&amp;nbsp;a Senior z/OS Base System Engineer, you will act as a key technical leader in&amp;nbsp;maintaining&amp;nbsp;and advancing our core mainframe operating system environment.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;We’re&amp;nbsp;looking for an experienced z/OS Systems Software Engineer&amp;nbsp;to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;design, develop, and improve&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;the core digital platform services we provide on z/OS. You will&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;apply a broad range of software engineering practices&lt;/strong&gt;, from analyzing system needs and developing new features to automated testing and deployment.&amp;nbsp;You’ll&amp;nbsp;ensure the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;quality, security, reliability, and compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;of our operating system solutions by implementing both functional and non-functional requirements.&amp;nbsp;You’ll&amp;nbsp;help&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;build observability&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;into our systems,&amp;nbsp;monitor&amp;nbsp;production health, resolve incidents, and perform root-cause analysis to improve stability. In addition, you will&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;monitor&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;optimize&amp;nbsp;Parallel&amp;nbsp;Sysplex&amp;nbsp;and Coupling Facility configurations&lt;/strong&gt;, ensuring high availability across mainframe clusters. As a senior engineer, you will make critical&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;technical decisions&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;and articulate your solution designs and proposals to stakeholders and technical leadership, serving as a trusted advisor on mainframe systems architecture. You will also&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;share knowledge and&amp;nbsp;expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;with colleagues, mentor junior engineers, and contribute to our engineering culture via code reviews, technical presentations, and participation in internal communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your team:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;In our agile operating model, crews are aligned to larger products and services that fulfill business needs through multiple autonomous pods.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;You’ll&amp;nbsp;be working in the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Mainframe Platform Core Services team&lt;/strong&gt;, a global crew responsible for mainframe infrastructure services and innovation. You will collaborate closely with other specialized mainframe engineering teams (e.g., DB2 Engineering and Online Systems Engineering for CICS/MQ) to deliver end-to-end reliable solutions. This role involves frequent interaction with operational teams across geographies (such as Switzerland, USA) to ensure alignment of system enhancements and operations. As a senior member,&amp;nbsp;you’ll&amp;nbsp;often&amp;nbsp;interface with&amp;nbsp;lead engineering boards and stakeholders to align mainframe platform improvements with business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your&amp;nbsp;expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;You have&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;10+ years’ experience in z/OS systems programming&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;or a similar senior engineering role. Your qualifications include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep knowledge of z/OS internals&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Expert skills in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;z/OS operating system architecture, design, and implementation&lt;/strong&gt;, with mastery of core z/OS components and subsystems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parallel&amp;nbsp;Sysplex&amp;nbsp;&amp;amp; Coupling Facility mastery&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Comprehensive experience in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Geographically Dispersed Parallel&amp;nbsp;Sysplex&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;(GDPS) operations and Coupling Facility management to ensure high availability and minimal outages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SMP/E and system installation&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;–&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on&amp;nbsp;expertise&amp;nbsp;with SMP/E&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;packaging, installation, and maintenance of z/OS software and operating system; capable of planning and executing complex system upgrades and ensuring OS currency (experience up to z/OS 3.1 preferred).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming &amp;amp; Scripting&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Proficiency in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;REXX&lt;/strong&gt;, TSO/ISPF, JCL, and other system programming languages; familiarity with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Assembler&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;coding is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance &amp;amp; Tools&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Strong&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;analytical skills&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;and thorough knowledge of z/OS performance tuning and system utilities; experience with IBM and non-IBM system management tools, monitoring, and problem determination utilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Management &amp;amp; Support&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Proven experience providing&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Level 3 support&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;for mainframe OS infrastructure, including diagnosing complex system&amp;nbsp;issues&amp;nbsp;and devising permanent solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Independent and Proactive&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– A self-driven engineer capable of working&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;independently&lt;/strong&gt;, taking initiative in&amp;nbsp;identifying&amp;nbsp;system improvements, and proactively addressing potential issues or vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Management &amp;amp; Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Good understanding of&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;change management processes&lt;/strong&gt;, with an ability to write clear system design and architecture documents (e.g., network and system design concept documents) and to guide technical changes from concept through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Learning &amp;amp; Strategic Thinking&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;– Eagerness to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;learn&amp;nbsp;new technologies&amp;nbsp;and practices&lt;/strong&gt;, reusing strategic platforms and standards; adept at evaluating options and making&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;long-term architectural decisions&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;that ensure sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;–&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Strong communication skills&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;are essential: fluent English (written and spoken) is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;mandatory&lt;/strong&gt;, and German language skills are a plus. You are comfortable presenting complex technical decisions to stakeholders and senior management. You also&amp;nbsp;demonstrate&amp;nbsp;leadership through mentoring and by influencing architecture and engineering best practices across the mainframe communit&lt;/p&gt;
